# wasp-lang/wasp v0.15.0 on GitHub
created: 2024-10-10, last updated: 2025-02-09, [Read more](https://newreleases.io/project/github/wasp-lang/wasp/release/v0.15.0)

Wasp 0.15.0 ships a preview feature that lets you define your app in
`main.wasp.ts` using TypeScript instead of in
`main.wasp` using the Wasp DSL.
So, instead of this:
```
app TodoApp {
wasp: {
version: "^0.15.0"
},
title: "TodoApp",
auth: {
userEntity: User,
methods: {
usernameAndPassword: {}
},
onAuthFailedRedirectTo: "/login"
route RootRoute { path: "/", to: MainPage }
page MainPage {
authRequired: true,
component: import { MainPage } from "@src/MainPage"
```
You can now write this:
```
improt { App } from 'wasp-config'
...
version: '^0.15.0',
},
title: 'TodoApp',
})
app.auth({
userEntity: 'User',
methods: {
usernameAndPassword: {}
},
onAuthFailedRedirectTo: '/login',
})
...
- If the user uses native DB types for the
`userEntity`, Wasp will use them correctly.

